:: Examples of the Scripting pages: a rule, and a function run when pages are linked.

:lua
```
nml.rule {
	name = "kbd",
	atoms = { ":kbd{", nml.capture("keys", nml.text, "string"), "}" },
	handler = function(m, out)
		out:element("code", { code = m.captures.keys, classes = { "kbd" } })
	end,
	doc = "**Keys** to press: `:kbd{Ctrl + C}`.",
	snippet = ":kbd{${1:keys}}",
}

-- How many pages the workspace has, when the page is linked.
function count()
	return tostring(#nml.pages())
end
```
